snippet.textDisplay:
@BurriedHistoryOfficial for an account that has ‘history’ in it I would expect a better understanding of technological progress. Initial research and development, which Boston Dynamic was doing is largely expensive, small run and not terribly effective. This was in part because Boston dynamics started decades ago. Recently they have made the move to more commercial ventures, but gather they are still largely about high end cutting edge technology research. 

These Chinese companies have come in just a few years ago, at a point where the various technologies are becoming feasible for deployment in commercial applications. They have not doubt used the r&d Boston dynamics and others like them to leapfrog to their current useable form. 

Not saying either are good or bad. I’m saying you are essentially comparing apples and oranges.

